NAME
       tail - output the last part of files

SYNOPSIS
       tail [-n [+]N] [-c [+]N] [-f] [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       Print the last 10 lines of each FILE.

OPTIONS
       -n N, -N
           output the last N lines; with +N start at line N

       -c N
           output the last N bytes; with +N start at byte N

       -f, --follow
           keep the file open and print data as it is appended; stop with
           Ctrl+C

       -q, -v
           never or always print headers

EXAMPLES
       tail -n 20 /root/log.txt
       tail -f /root/build.log

SEE ALSO
       head(1), less(1)
